      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of an angiographically documented fistula between the circumflex coronary artery and a left strial appendage thrombus in a patient with mitral stenosis, flow from which can be demonstrated solely by a color doppler transesophageal echocardiogram. Evaluation of catheter derived hemodynamics and angiographic flow patterns reveals a heretofore undescribed physiologic property of coronary to atrial shunts in patients with mitral stenosis."},
